# npm (only used for the shared midrash-viewer-core package; the built
# bundle is vendored under vendor/midrash-viewer-core and IS committed)
node_modules/

# Chasdei David: our OCR of the Vagshal "חסדי דוד השלם" edition, which is NOT a
# plain facsimile of a public-domain printing -- it advertises itself as newly
# prepared and annotated, and its Seder Taharot was first published from
# manuscript only in recent decades. Pardo himself died in 1790, so the
# commentary is long out of copyright; the EDITION we transcribed is the problem.
# Until it is re-sourced from a pre-1929 printing, this stays local. Tekhelet
# Mordechai (HebrewBooks scan of Pakš 1895) is public and IS committed.
#
# Exported by editionsDigitization/export_commentary_layers.py. The viewer simply
# shows no tab for a commentary whose file is absent, so a checkout without these
# needs no special casing.
data/commentaries-ocr/ChasdeiDavid_*.json

# Morphological-analysis lexicon: attestation counts and analyses for apparatus
# words, derived from an external tagged reference corpus that cannot be
# redistributed. Built outside this repo; the generators degrade gracefully
# when it is absent.
data/morphology_lexicon.json
